         text="Toyotomi Hideyoshi had an earth rampart with a moat outside thrown round Kyoto, 22.5 km long, planted with bamboo. In the same years he cut new north-south streets through the old square blocks, moved the temples to Teramachi and rebuilt the palace: the shape of Kyoto to this day.",
